  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reverse Trade Mission - ASEAN Cybersecurity and Digital Solutions Reverse Trade Mission Series, through Business Council for International Understanding</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ASEAN Cybersecurity and Digital Solutions Reverse Trade Mission Series consists of two separate and distinct RTMs designed to familiarize leaders from financial institutions and utility companies in the ASEAN region with state-of-the-art U.S. ICT technologies, services, and best practice for cybersecurity and digital solutions. The primary objective of the RTM series is to support the capacity of ASEAN banks and utility companies to mitigate risks to digital infrastructure and optimize operations by enhancing their cybersecurity and digital capabilities. This memorandum serves as a no-cost modification to the decision and project memoranda for the ASEAN Cybersecurity and Digital Solutions Reverse Trade Mission Series (USTDA Activity No. 2019-31018A). The change allows USTDA to invite Solomon Islands central bank representatives to participate in the Reverse Trade Mission as delegates.</narrative>
  </description>
